  using the base budget <verbatim|P>, selected profile <verbatim|\<Xi\>>'s
  clip/width/paths, kinetic parameter, <verbatim|Time.credit G \<Xi\> *
  \<delta\>E>, and base support exponent plus two. <verbatim|Time.Same \<Xi\>
  P> matches power, order and support exponent. The receipt is raised; the
  price is not evaluated at the raised budget.>>|<row|<cell|Rate price
  meaning>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Progress.DirectedRecipe.Payments.Rates>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Progress/DIRECTED_RECIPE/Tender.lean>>|<cell|Requires
  nonnegative hard/soft goals, soft goal at most one,
  <verbatim|(2B+1)^4*(exp(kappa)*hard+2*soft)\<leq\>1>, and quote price
  <verbatim|Bid.quote kappa (exp(kappa)*hard+2*soft)\<leq\>goal>.>>|<row|<cell|Fiberwise
  paid-family aggregation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.towing>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accent.lean>>|<cell|Preserves
  coefficient-majorant price and support-hit ledger under summation over
  fibers.>>|<row|<cell|Menu singleton price/nilpotence/charge
  recovery>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Menu.virtue>, <verbatim|.paid>,
  <verbatim|.purchase>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Buys.lean>>|<cell|Nonempty
  marker mode gives zero quiet coefficient and self-overlap nilpotence;
  weighted price is at most one and fee multiplication recovers the charged
  singleton.>>|<row|<cell|Exact per-box canopy
  identities>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Merge.Photo.shade>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Menu.Canopy.buyer>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Shaded.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Copse.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Magma.selfie>
  gives quiet profile; <verbatim|Magma.scored> expands the push as
  exponential action times the pass of the summed spine times the full field
  polynomial. <verbatim|Photo.shade> consumes the exact per-menu singleton
  jet identity, the paid <verbatim|Towed> receipts, and square-zero menu
  polynomials. Its coefficient extraction uses <verbatim|Accent.quality> and
  sums only the singleton terms; higher field coefficients remain
  products.>>>>>

  <section|Quantitative proof notes and limits><label|quantitative-proof-notes-and-limits>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|Palette.lucent> is a selected source estimate, not a
    consequence of the fee formula alone. <verbatim|Palette.sizes> derives
    summability by the shared <verbatim|Charity.everyoneN> counting result
    with the fragrance library and its separation hypotheses. The manuscript
    must not infer global summability by summing a pointwise root inequality
    over the infinite lattice.

    <item><verbatim|Many.usable> doubles <verbatim|lace> and
    <verbatim|lucent>; this gives exact output allowance
    <verbatim|2*pledgeA/(1-sailUp)>. Its payment exponent is the sum of the
    earned exponent and the selected allowance. The rooted support set is the
    full <verbatim|bookFoot> used by the source. <verbatim|Charity.everyoneN>
    invokes <verbatim|YM.Push.AbsoluteSums.Product.everyone_ne>, which turns
    the pointwise rooted hit into a total fee sum with explicit factor
    <verbatim|\|Site(c)\|=c^4>; no infinite-lattice sum over roots is taken.

    <item>The two activity rows are distinct. <verbatim|Stage.usable> uses
    <verbatim|Signed.crowd>, whose <verbatim|plants> receipt is
    <verbatim|Mallow.cools> (<verbatim|softNeed>) with an ordinary allowance
    at most <verbatim|betaF^(-1/8)>. <verbatim|Paprika.crowd2> instead uses
    <verbatim|Pungent> and the raised <verbatim|Spicy.june> receipt
    (<verbatim|opens> at the base budget/profile) for its second rate clause.
    Its first rate clause separately uses the raised precursor allowance at
    most <verbatim|exp(coverTicket)*betaF^(-1/8)>; this is not the final
    <verbatim|opens> price. Keep their different rate clauses and allowance
    hypotheses.

    <item>The widening proof is the zero extension along the injective
    activity-label map: old coefficients are retained on its image and all
    other coefficients are zero. Physical supports at retained labels are
    unchanged, so the same rooted-hit receipt is transported. The widening
    retains the exponent allowance; harvesting consumes the reserved exponent
    unit. <verbatim|Motion.harvest> then uses the hard/soft fusion price and
    the rooted forest budget. Its local algebra is expanded in the
    manuscript, while remaining analytic receipts are identified as source
    inputs.

    <item>The singleton jet identity used by <verbatim|Photo.shade> is
    discharged in sibling unit <verbatim|rg-menu-jets.tex>, equation
    <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-menu-jet-proof>. It follows from the actual
    empty/singleton interpolation identities and differentiability of the
    one-menu final path. The menu fee equals the tuning coefficient in the
    selected bidding step. The paid score majorants and door-volume receipt
    remain explicit quantitative inputs to the countable coefficient and
    hinge sums.

    <item>The soft/hard fused gas calculation is cited from sibling draft
    unit <verbatim|manuscript/existence/soft-log-fusion.tex>, section
    <verbatim|sec:soft-log-fusion>, equations
    <verbatim|eq:fusion-gas-identity> and <verbatim|eq:fusion-site-output>.
    It gives the exact flag-compatible component bijection and the site-price
    estimate used by <verbatim|Motion.harvest>; this chapter does not
    reproduce the component bijection.

    <item>The final field polynomial is indexed by boxes <verbatim|(P_p,Q_p)>
    with full support <verbatim|P_p> and assigned flag
    <verbatim|Q_p\<subseteq\>P_p>. Families require disjoint full supports
    and have flag union equal to the selected support mode. Nonzero
    compatible activity terms cannot share a barcode because its full support
    is nonempty; grouping by barcode therefore preserves the support-disjoint
    family, and absolute convergence justifies the countable regrouping.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Commands actually run><label|commands-actually-run>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|rg -n 'lemma (usable\|crowd\|listens\|valueP\|june\|funds\|fair\|lace\|sizes\|lucent\|within_alpha\|owns)'
    Lean/YM/...> \V located the producers and their immediate dependencies.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n> reads of <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/{Stage,Signed,Paprika,Dreams,Steps,Echo,Record,Motion,Ginger,Shaded,Copse,Magma,Accent,Buys,Switch,SwitchProd,SwitchCost,Mirrored,Silo,Bouquet,Coffer,Tinder}.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Pep.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Progress/DIRECTED_RECIPE/Tender.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/RG_NEXT_COMPLETE_REPEATABLE_NONLINEAR_STEP/Mallow/{Eco,Brisk,Reseve,Seminal}.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/UVNext/COUPLING_RESET/Precision.lean>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>, and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/{ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe,NativeComponentRecipe}.lean>.

    <item>Inspected exact raised estimate definitions and call in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Ginger.lean> and
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Paprika.lean>; the output is at the raised
    point but <verbatim|Spicy.opens> is priced on the base budget and base
    selected parameters.

    <item>Read <verbatim|manuscript/existence/soft-log-fusion.tex> in the
    parent integration checkout for its independent passed labels
    <verbatim|sec:soft-log-fusion>, <verbatim|eq:fusion-gas-identity>, and
    <verbatim|eq:fusion-site-output>.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was attempted; it
    stopped because this isolated claim unit has no
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>. No Lean build, full
    repository build, or manuscript compile was run.
  </itemize-minus>

